Deployment Diagram
A Deployment Diagram is a UML (Unified Modeling Language) diagram used to represent the physical deployment of hardware and software components in a system.

It shows:

Hardware devices (nodes)

Software components

Network connections

System architecture

It is mainly used in:

System deployment planning

Network architecture

Distributed systems

Definition
A Deployment Diagram describes:

Physical arrangement of system components

Communication between hardware devices

Installation of software on hardware

It gives the physical view of the system.

Main Components of Deployment Diagram
1. Node
A node represents a physical device or execution environment.

Examples:
Server

Computer

Mobile Device

Database Server

